---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Hero from '../../components/Hero.astro';
import { company } from '../../content/site';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="International Car Shipping & RORO"
  description="RoRo, LoLo, and container vehicle shipping with African port coverage."
  image="/images/car.jpg"
>
  <Hero
    compact
    brand="RORO"
    headline="Vehicle and heavy equipment shipping done right."
    support="RoRo, LoLo, or container — door-to-door and port-to-port options for cars and machinery."
    image="/images/car.jpg"
    secondaryCta={{ label: 'Get a Quote', href: '/quote' }}
  />

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container content reveal">
      <p>
        We help transport excess baggage, earth-moving equipment, generators, mining equipment, heavy
        machinery, transport vehicles, boats and yachts on trailers or cradles, cranes, and plant
        assemblies to your destination with precision.
      </p>
      <p>
        When transporting a vehicle, there are three main alternatives: <strong>RoRo</strong>,
        <strong>LoLo</strong>, or <strong>container</strong>.
      </p>

      <h2>RoRo (Roll-on / Roll-off)</h2>
      <p>
        Often the easiest and most cost-effective way to ship a vehicle overseas — minimal lifting and
        no block-and-brace into a container. After the vehicle is driven onto the vessel, it is secured
        on wind- and watertight decks. We provide door-to-door and port-to-port services for cargo that
        can roll on and off, including oversized and heavy-lift cargo where suitable.
      </p>

      <h2>LoLo (Lift-on / Lift-off)</h2>
      <p>
        The vehicle is loaded and unloaded by crane. For static cargo that is not self-propelled, a
        modular transporter such as a MAFI trailer can be used. LoLo is a strong choice for inoperable
        large vehicles and equipment.
      </p>

      <h2>Container shipping</h2>
      <p>
        Containers are highly secure and tamper-resistant, offering greater protection from transit
        damage — often preferred for high-value luxury cars in 20′ or 40′ ocean containers.
      </p>

      <h2>Ports we service include</h2>
      <ul class="ports">
        <li>Durban – South Africa</li>
        <li>Walvis Bay – Namibia</li>
        <li>Beira – Mozambique</li>
        <li>Mombasa – Kenya</li>
        <li>Dar es Salaam – Tanzania</li>
        <li>Lagos – Nigeria</li>
        <li>Abidjan – Ivory Coast</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Typical documents for vehicle clearance</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Original bill of lading</li>
        <li>Original vehicle registration</li>
        <li>Purchase invoice</li>
        <li>Shipping invoice</li>
        <li>Completed power of attorney (POA) form</li>
      </ul>

      <p>
        For booking or queries, call
        <a href={company.phone.mobileHref}>{company.phone.mobile}</a>
        or email
        <a href={company.emailHref}>{company.email}</a>.
      </p>

      <a class="btn btn-primary" href="/quote">Request a vehicle shipping quote</a>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .content {
    max-width: 72ch;
  }

  h2 {
    margin-top: 2rem;
    font-size: 1.55rem;
  }

  ul {
    padding-left: 1.2rem;
    color: var(--muted);
  }

  .ports {
    columns: 2;
    gap: 2rem;
  }

  .btn {
    margin-top: 1.5rem;
  }

  a {
    color: var(--brand-deep);
    font-weight: 700;
  }

  @media (max-width: 600px) {
    .ports {
      columns: 1;
    }
  }
</style>
